    "lawCode": "Amd §75-b, Civ Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1096\n\nSPONSOR: LIU\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the civil service law, in relation to the definition of\na public employee or employee\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill will amend CVS-75b to include all employees of judges,\njustices of the unified court system, and members of the legislature as\n\"public employees,\" so that workers may report misconduct without fear\nof retaliation.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill will include all employees of judges, justices of the unified\ncourt system, and members of the legislature within the definition of a\n\"public employee\" or \"employee.\"\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMany acts of workplace misconduct, including sexual assault, are carried\nout by those who are in a position of power. Employees who are aware of\nsuch acts are often afraid to report such misconduct for fear that they\nwill lose their jobs or face retaliation. This bill will ensure that\nemployees who disclose violations of law or improper conduct to a\ngovernmental body will be protected from retaliation or disciplinary\naction.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
